KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ forward of an array lvalue keeps the array reference type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
type mismatch
dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.static.cast]/3 + [dcl.ref]/6: with T deduced as `const char
(&)[4]' from a string literal argument, `static_cast<T &&>(t)' in
std::forward is a cast to `const char (&)[4]' (reference collapsing) whose
operand is the array lvalue -- an identity conversion.  static_typecast
does not accept a cast to a reference-to-array type from an array lvalue
("type mismatch on static_cast: operand type 'const char [4l]', cast type
'const char [4l] &'") and forward's body is dropped; every perfect-forwarded
string literal then reads as nondet (audit residue item 9, round 162: the
remaining `forward' drops of the corpus, e.g. std::string constructed
through emplace).
